Add input page for Develop Execution Plan item of the ADLC folder.
When clicked it should bring up the page where the user can input the Fields

Agent Harness (this one is mandatory) use Codex by default
Agent Model (this one is optional)
Agent Intelligence (this one is optional)

Project Workspace folder (this one is mandatory).
by default it should be folder project root folder

Project Description folder (this one is mandatory). By default it should be <Project Workspace folder>/docs/project_description
Project Execution Plan file (this one is mandatory). By default it should be <Project Workspace folder>/docs/project-execution-plan.md
Project Backlog folder (this one is mandatory). By default it should be <Project Workspace folder>/docs/backlog
Project Architecture folder file (this one is mandatory). By default it should be <Project Workspace folder>/docs/architecture

Then it shows a field called Agent Script Path (this one is mandatory)

Then it has a run button (that only gets enabled when the mandatory fields are filled). When the button is clicked; then the script at Agent Script Path should be run with parameters

--execution-plan <Project Execution Plan file>
--project-description-dir <Project Description folder> (only if not empty)  
--architecture-dir <Project Architecture folder> (only if not empty) 
--backlog-dir <Project Backlog folder> (only if not empty)   
--workspace <Project Workspace folder>
--harness <Agent Harness>
--model <Agent Model> (only if not empty) 
--intelligence <Agent Intelligence> (only if not empty) 



Always save the last used settings so next time the page is launched it takes those values for the project in use.

Follow the same pattern used for other ADLC items
